{
  "dom_id": "step-q105883",
  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "If $S={0,1,2,3,4,5}$, which collection of subsets of $S$ is a partition of $S?$",
  "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $S$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $S$ where every element of $S$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{0,2,4},{1,3,5}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${\u2205,{0,2,4},{1,3,5}}$ is not a partition because the subset $\u2205$ is empty.\n\n- ${{0,1,2,3,4,5,6}}$ is not a partition because the element $6$ does not appear in $S.$\n\n- ${{0,1},{2},{4,5}}$ is not a partition because the element $3\\in S$ does not appear in any subset.\n\n- ${{0,1},{1,2,3,4,5}}$ is not a partition because the element $1$ appears in two subsets.",
